# Rust build output
/target
**/*.rs.bk

# Commit workflow scratch (must stay untracked — see COMMIT.md)
git_message_brief.txt

# Generated artifacts are regenerated locally, never tracked (see COMMIT.md)
/generated

# Documented scratch/output root. `ROADMAP.md` §10.1's worked example writes here
# (`archogen resolve … --out build/plan.json`, `archogen build … --out build/periodic-three`), and
# so do the book's target and S0 chapters and `scripts/target_emulator.sh --dump-dtb`. Ignored for
# the reason `PROGRAM.12` gives for harness scratch: never committed, and never left untracked
# either, because "handoff-ready" means a clean `git status`. A reader who follows the roadmap's own
# example must not thereby dirty the tree. Owned by leaf `PROGRAM.22`.
/build

# Logs & OS cruft
*.log
.DS_Store

# Note: Cargo.lock is intentionally NOT ignored — binary/application projects should
# commit it for reproducible builds. If this becomes a library-only workspace, add it.

# mdBook build output (regenerated by `make book`)
/docs/book/book

# LinkedSpec application-owned build/data root (each issue's own SETUP.md, under
# docs/feedback/linkedspec/issues/, describes the storage this holds)
/.app-data/
docs/feedback/**/.repro-work/

# Harness-local scratch: the permissions and state an AI harness records per project while a
# session runs. It is one session's approval decisions, not a project decision, so it is never
# committed — and never left untracked either, because "handoff-ready" means a clean
# `git status`. A harness config this project deliberately shares is added with `git add -f`.
# Scoped to the harness measured here (leaf PROGRAM.12); add a line when another one appears.
/.qwen/
# The template's incoming copies, written by scripts/update_scaffold.sh beside nothing of ours (bedrock 0.10.0,
# adopted by leaf PROGRAM.26): read them, take what you want by hand, then `rm -rf .bedrock-incoming`.
.bedrock-incoming/
